{
  "name": "Draft LinkedIn openers with AI and approve each one by email before saving",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "trig",
      "name": "Every weekday morning",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
        0,
        440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "hours",
              "hoursInterval": 24
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "cfg",
      "name": "Who you are looking for",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        260,
        440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "a0",
              "name": "searchQuery",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "head of operations logistics"
            },
            {
              "id": "a1",
              "name": "whatYouSell",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "route planning software for delivery fleets"
            },
            {
              "id": "a2",
              "name": "approver",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "you@example.com"
            },
            {
              "id": "a3",
              "name": "maxItems",
              "type": "number",
              "value": 20
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "a1",
      "name": "Find matching people",
      "type": "@apify/n8n-nodes-apify.apify",
      "position": [
        540,
        440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "memory": 1024,
        "actorId": "dami_studio~linkedin-profile-search-scraper",
        "timeout": 300,
        "resource": "Actors",
        "operation": "Run actor and get dataset",
        "customBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ searchQuery: $json.searchQuery, maxItems: $json.maxItems }) }}",
        "maxTotalChargeUsd": 1
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "flt",
      "name": "Keep the ones with a real headline",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.filter",
      "position": [
        800,
        440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 3,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "f1",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ (($json.headline || \"\").toString().length) > 15 }}",
              "rightValue": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.3
    },
    {
      "id": "dd",
      "name": "Skip anyone already contacted",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.removeDuplicates",
      "position": [
        1060,
        440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {
          "scope": "node",
          "historySize": 100000
        },
        "operation": "removeItemsSeenInPreviousExecutions",
        "dedupeValue": "={{ $json.profileUrl || $json.url }}"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "ch",
      "name": "Draft an opener",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "position": [
        1320,
        440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=You sell: {{ $('Who you are looking for').first().json.whatYouSell }}\n\nThis person came up in a search:\nName: {{ $json.fullName || $json.name }}\nHeadline: {{ $json.headline }}\nCompany: {{ $json.currentCompany || $json.company }}\n\nWrite one opening line you could actually send them. Reference something specific in their\nheadline. No flattery, no \"I hope this finds you well\", no pitch in the first line. Under 30\nwords. If their headline is too vague to say anything specific, return exactly: skip\n\nReturn ONLY the line, nothing else.",
        "promptType": "define"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.9
    },
    {
      "id": "llm",
      "name": "OpenAI chat model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "position": [
        1320,
        660
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "gpt-5-mini"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "appr",
      "name": "Ask you before anything is saved",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "position": [
        1580,
        440
      ],
      "webhookId": "approval-gate-46",
      "parameters": {
        "sendTo": "={{ $('Who you are looking for').first().json.approver }}",
        "message": "=Person: {{ $json.fullName || $json.name }}\nHeadline: {{ $json.headline }}\n\nDrafted opener:\n{{ $json.text }}\n\nApprove to add them to the sheet. Decline to drop them.",
        "options": {
          "limitWaitTime": {
            "values": {
              "resumeUnit": "hours",
              "resumeAmount": 12
            }
          }
        },
        "subject": "=Approve this opener? {{ $json.fullName || $json.name }}",
        "operation": "sendAndWait",
        "approvalOptions": {
          "values": {
            "approvalType": "double"
          }
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.1
    },
    {
      "id": "iff",
      "name": "Did you approve it?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        1840,
        440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "i1",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.data.approved === true }}",
              "rightValue": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "sh",
      "name": "Approved go to the sheet",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "position": [
        2100,
        310
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "columns": {
          "value": {},
          "mappingMode": "autoMapInputData",
          "matchingColumns": []
        },
        "options": {},
        "operation": "append",
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": ""
        },
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": ""
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.7
    },
    {
      "id": "nop",
      "name": "Declined ones stop here",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "position": [
        2100,
        570
      ],
      "parameters": {},
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "opt-slack",
      "name": "Optional: ask in Slack instead of email",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "position": [
        1580,
        880
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=Approve opener for {{ $json.fullName || $json.name }}?\n{{ $json.text }}",
        "select": "channel",
        "channelId": "#sales",
        "otherOptions": {}
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.3
    },
    {
      "id": "opt-http",
      "name": "Optional: push approved ones to your CRM",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "position": [
        1840,
        880
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://example.com/your-crm",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 20000
        },
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json) }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json"
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    },
    {
      "id": "st0",
      "name": "Sticky Note s0",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -40,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### 1. Every morning\n\nRuns once a day. Nothing here posts, emails or messages the prospect - the only thing that leaves the building is one email to YOU."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st1",
      "name": "Sticky Note s1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        220,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### 2. Who you want\n\nThe search, what you sell, and the address that gets the approval request. The model reads \"what you sell\" when drafting."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st2",
      "name": "Sticky Note s2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        480,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### 3. Find them\n\nA LinkedIn people search, no login. Returns public headline and current company, capped by max items and a max charge."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st3",
      "name": "Sticky Note s3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        740,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### 4. Two cheap filters\n\nDrop anyone whose headline is too thin to personalise from, then drop anyone this workflow already showed you in a previous run."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st4",
      "name": "Sticky Note s4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1000,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### 5. Draft, do not send\n\nOne opening line per person, grounded in their headline. Returns \"skip\" when the headline is too vague to say anything real."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st5",
      "name": "Sticky Note s5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1260,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### 6. The gate\n\nThis is the node the workflow exists for. It emails you the draft and PAUSES until you click approve or decline. Nothing is written while it waits."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st6",
      "name": "Sticky Note s6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1520,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### 7. Your click decides\n\nApproved rows land in the sheet. Declined ones stop at a No-Op so the run still finishes cleanly and you can see how many you rejected."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st-opt",
      "name": "Sticky Note optional",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1540,
        760
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 210,
        "content": "## Optional - other shapes\n\nWired to nothing on purpose. **Slack** if approvals belong in a channel rather than your inbox, **HTTP Request** to push the approved ones into a CRM instead of a sheet."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "st-desc",
      "name": "Sticky Note overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -680,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 1420,
        "content": "## Draft LinkedIn openers with AI, then approve each one by email before it is saved\n\nFinds people matching a search, drafts one opening line each, and emails them to you one at a time. Nothing is written anywhere until you click approve.\n\n**Who is this for?**\nAnyone doing outbound who wants the drafting automated but not the judgement, and who has been burned by a bot that sent something embarrassing.\n\n**What problem is this workflow solving?**\nMost lead workflows write straight to a sheet or a sequencer, so the first time a human reads the AI output is after it has been acted on. That is the wrong order. This one stops at a human: the model does the tedious part, and you keep the decision that matters.\n\n**What this workflow does**\n- Runs a LinkedIn people search for the role you describe, with no login.\n- Drops anyone whose headline is too thin to personalise from, and anyone shown to you before.\n- Drafts one opening line per person, grounded in their actual headline.\n- Emails you that draft and **pauses the execution** until you approve or decline.\n- Approved rows go to a sheet. Declined ones stop dead.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Put your search, what you sell, and your own email address in the second node.\n2. Connect Apify, OpenAI, Gmail and Google Sheets credentials.\n3. Run it once by hand. You get an email per person - approve one to see the sheet fill.\n\n**Requirements**\nApify, an OpenAI key, Gmail (for the approval email, not for mailing prospects), and a Google Sheet.\n\n**How to customize this workflow to your needs**\nThe wait is capped at 12 hours in the approval node options. Past that the execution stops and nothing is written, which is the safe direction. The approval type is `double`, so you get approve AND decline buttons; switch it to single if you only want a confirm.\n\n**Good to know**\nOne email per person does not scale to hundreds. At 20 a day it is a two-minute inbox job; at 200 it will bury you, so lower max items rather than batching approvals. The execution also sits genuinely open while it waits, so an unapproved run shows as running until the 12-hour cap expires."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
